{#
  The documentation chrome.

  `PageContentGenerator` hard-codes this filename and every template under
  `pages/` extends it, so it stays as a named seam even though the page chrome
  itself lives in `_layout.jinja` — the arrangement Stilyagi and Weaver use.

  What it adds over the layout is docs-only: the scroll-spy and copy-button
  scripts, and the column flex a docs sidebar needs to fill the viewport. Both
  were defaults on the layout until the homepage had to override them to
  nothing; a page opts into the docs chrome by extending this file rather than
  opting out of it by emptying two blocks.
#}
{% extends "_layout.jinja" %}

{% block page_scripts %}
    <script defer src="/netsuke/assets/js/docs-scrollspy.js"></script>
    <script defer src="/netsuke/assets/js/copy-buttons.js"></script>
{% endblock %}

{% block body_class %} flex flex-col min-h-screen{% endblock %}
